description:
Fox Squirrel - Sciurus niger
This might have been a mating chase. Squirrels emerged rapidly from right to cross boardwalk. Smaller one, appearing to be a male, turned around when it saw me and disappeared back to the right. Between the two frames I have an image of the male (-;
In both of these images the large tarsal pads on the rear feet are visible. I think this is a characteristic that can help distinguish Fox Squirrel from Eastern Gray Squirrel where one cannot judge size, or where color of pelage is similar.
